{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact f0eed793bed4e8ddf778980bc2970690841b39d4 on request/i7-object-key-probe-decision, sole changed path notes/2026-09-05-capability-context-contract.md, reporting artifact c457a25a, under review request #4234 (d2f7d39d) and source request #4228 (25fb8752), adopted proposal 077daf8d ratified by hugh (ratifier) in 8b3a8507. Reviewed in a detached checkout of my own at the exact head; one commit over main 756ce43a; git diff --check clean; frontmatter adds #4228 as a base; the historical sections and the declaration through the eight gates are otherwise unchanged apart from the four cross-references at lines 3, 48-52, 236-237, 247-249 and 387-388 that point to the new section.\n\nConditions of #4228 and proposal 077daf8d, checked against the new section at lines 509-592: compile/admission classification by a complete bounded walk of the admitted AST including nested expressions and all branches, on resolved direct selected-extension calls, not text or execution; omission of the entire preliminary whole-input evaluation including pure work, lexical effects and errors, also when the selected call is dormant; no dry-run, memoization, result reuse, alternate frame or uncharged speculative dispatch; one normal evaluation at each existing per-item/tuple semantic point with normal scope, checks, charging, failure ordering and complete discovery before values; extension-free keys keep the legacy preliminary evaluation; a call only in a group value does not change the key rule; confinement unchanged; the compatibility exception is explicit for both mixed-key cases and for dormant branches; per-item T1003, undefined keys, source order, D1009, lexical scopes and first-encounter order stay; empty/null/tuple discovery keeps one semantic evaluation of the virtual undefined item, charged once, with no second probe; the fixture table gives exactly the eleven required results with ordered call traces and the required choices (two-item direct key two calls not three, whole-input-only branch zero not one, {($)\u003e1 ? 7 : (\"k\"):$} -\u003e {\"k\":[1,2]} with k,k, the dormant-branch key -\u003e {\"k\":[1,2]} with zero calls, the extension-free control keeps preliminary T1003, the invalid per-item key keeps per-item T1003 with zero calls); the lexical pair is stated with baseline {\"2\":3,\"3\":3} and required {\"1\":2,\"2\":2}, both zero calls; nested key/group, tuple/reduce, colliding keys failing before any value, omission/extra-dispatch/misclassification/skipped-charge controls and the paired extension-free corpus are required as gate-3 extensions, not replacements; identity accounting names core.jsonata, grammar, dialect and corpus components, keeps exactly ten components and old-identity recognition, revalidates stored programs before replay writes with refusal leaving projection and frontier unchanged, keeps the acknowledged reset boundary, four stages and eight gates, adds no component or migration; no publication, admission, live operation, reset or release is authorized; implementation, pin and callers stay on #4043.\n\nBaseline evidence: I re-ran the attached baseline-probe.go myself in a fresh module pinned to github.com/jsonata-go/jsonata v0.0.0-20250709164031-599f35f32e5f (go.sum h1:JnGon8QHtmjFPq0NcSu8OTEnQDDEgFME7gtj/NkjCUo=); all fourteen outputs, error strings and ordered call traces are identical to baseline-results.jsonl, including both lexical cases. I also read the pinned source: v206/jsonata.go evaluates pair[0] against the whole input once, at itemIndex 0, only for object constructors and not for the reduce form, swallowing any error and raising T1003 only for a non-string result; that matches the note's description of the probe, explains the three-versus-two and one-versus-zero counts, and confirms that omitting it removes only that evaluation. The proposed results in the table are requirements for #4043, not measured behaviour, and the note says so. Provenance: the artifact's eighteen actual bases are the #4228 promise 8c1167d9, the published note 727ab6a7 and the sixteen implementation artifacts listed in source-provenance.json; all sixteen are live, none stale, and each file is byte-identical at f0eed793 to the commit its artifact names; the 22 local source links in validation.json resolve to the stated lines in my checkout. The head-news list after the request names no other head.\n\nArchitecture: affected layers are the jsonataddl evaluator layer (compile, confine, evaluate, identity, dialect, input contract, load, values, authorizer, application), the engine and projection layer that consumes it, and the MCP tools surface; the head changes documentation only and preserves every implemented contract, so no reference page needs a contract update. The decision narrows the legacy object-constructor preliminary probe for extension-bearing keys only and leaves the reduce/group form, which has no preliminary probe, untouched.\n\nSecurity: the trust boundary of the extension path is unchanged; classification uses resolved selected-call identity rather than text, so a provider cannot be reached through a differently spelled reference, and the no-reference/no-shadow/no-partial confinement stands; the rule removes an uncharged speculative provider invocation instead of adding one, so fixed call limits and charging are strengthened, not weakened; the compatibility exception is disclosed rather than hidden, including that omitted pure lexical effects can change later keys; the bound on the classification walk is the admitted AST, which existing admission limits already bound; failure modes (per-item T1003, D1009, undefined keys) keep their existing ordering; stored programs are revalidated before replay writes and refusal leaves state unchanged. Adoption basis: proposal 077daf8d rests on the artifact and was ratified by hugh, who holds ratifier, in the effective act 8b3a8507; the review request follows adoption and asks for decision review only, not runtime